{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevKbJUNYfUezzSc4zUWX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete understanding of the codebase. Let me summarize my findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity (Order.kt:11) lacks a status field\n- Shipment entity (Shipment.kt:9) already has status field with enum ShipmentStatus (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- OrderController (OrderController.kt:15-46) only has POST (create) and GET endpoints\n- ShipmentController (ShipmentController.kt:20-56) only has POST (create) and GET endpoints  \n- OrderRepository (OrderRepository.kt:10-27) is an in-memory store with no filtering\n- ShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27) is an in-memory store with no findByOrderId method\n- ErrorCode enum (ApiError.kt:31-37) has: ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n- Exception handling follows ApiException hierarchy with ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler (GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28) centralizes error response formatting\n\n**Conventions observed:**\n- Error handling via ApiException hierarchy with centralized GlobalExceptionHandler\n- Spring REST conventions: @RestController, @RequestMapping, @PostMapping, @GetMapping\n- In-memory repositories autowired as @Repository beans\n- Request DTOs separate from entities (CreateOrderRequest, CreateShipmentRequest)\n- Tests use MockMvc and assert both HTTP status and error envelope structure ($.error.code, $.error.message)\n- All existing tests pass (13 tests, 0 failures)\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt - must add status field and OrderStatus enum\n2. OrderController.kt - must add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint\n3. OrderRepository.kt - may need methods to support cancel operation\n4. ShipmentRepository.kt - must add findByOrderId method to query shipments by order\n5. ShipmentController.kt - must check order status before creating shipment\n6. ApiError.kt - must add new error codes for cancel-specific conflicts\n7. OrderControllerTest.kt - must add tests for cancel endpoint behavior\n8. ShipmentControllerTest.kt - must add tests for shipment creation on cancelled order (if not in existing tests)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Shipment creation must validate order exists and is not cancelled before delegating to repository\n- Cancel must be all-or-nothing: if any shipment is CONFIRMED, entire operation fails and no state changes\n- Concurrent access to order/shipment stores during cancel operation with multiple shipment updates\n- Idempotency: cancelling already-cancelled order must succeed without error\n- Tests must verify all edge cases (non-existent order, confirmed shipments, already cancelled, etc.)\n\n**Open questions:**\n- What specific error codes should be added to ErrorCode enum for:\n  - Attempting to cancel an order with a CONFIRMED shipment? (e.g., ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT or similar)\n  - Attempting to create shipment for a CANCELLED order? (e.g., ORDER_CANCELLED)\n\nBased on the requirement \"Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API\" and existing code patterns, I'll add meaningful error codes to the enum.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add `status: OrderStatus` field and create `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values. Update data class to include status.\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** - Add two new error codes to ErrorCode enum:\n   - `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` - when cancelling order with confirmed shipment\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` - when creating shipment for cancelled order\n\n3. **OrderRepository.kt** - Add method `findByOrderId` if needed for cancel logic, but likely not needed since we'll fetch order directly first.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to get all shipments for an order during cancel operation.\n\n5. **OrderController.kt** - Add:\n   - Inject ShipmentRepository \n   - Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that:\n     - Checks if order exists (404 if not)\n     - If already CANCELLED, return order as-is (idempotent)\n     - Check all shipments for that order\n     - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT (409, no changes)\n     - Otherwise, mark order as CANCELLED and all CREATED shipments as CANCELLED\n     - Return the cancelled order\n\n6. **ShipmentController.kt** - Modify POST /shipments endpoint to:\n   - Fetch the order before creating shipment\n   - Check order exists (keep current 404 behavior for non-existent order as requirement states)\n   - Check order is not CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED (409) if cancelled\n   - Proceed with shipment creation\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add tests for:\n   - Cancel ACTIVE order successfully\n   - Cancel already CANCELLED order (idempotent)\n   - Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 with ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT\n   - Cancel non-existent order returns 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add test for:\n   - Create shipment for CANCELLED order returns 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- *Alternative 1*: Add OrderStatus as a separate service/handler class. Rejected: Too complex for this domain, status is simple state on entity.\n- *Alternative 2*: Use string status instead of enum. Rejected: Type safety and readability; existing code uses enums for similar concepts (ShipmentStatus).\n- *Alternative 3*: Create new repository methods for cancel. Rejected: Simpler to handle in controller with direct repository access.\n- *Alternative 4*: Not add new error codes, reuse VALIDATION_FAILED. Rejected: Violates \"error responses consistent with API\" and loses semantic meaning.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Success case - Cancel ACTIVE order:*\n1. Request: POST /orders/O-123/cancel\n2. OrderController.cancel(orderId):\n   - Fetch order from repo → exists and status=ACTIVE\n   - Query ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(\"O-123\") → returns list [S-1(CREATED), S-2(CREATED)]\n   - No CONFIRMED shipments → proceed\n   - Update order status ACTIVE → CANCELLED\n   - Update each shipment status CREATED → CANCELLED\n   - Save all to repository\n   - Return updated Order with status=CANCELLED\n3. Response: 200 OK with order body\n\n*Success case - Cancel already CANCELLED order:*\n1. Request: POST /orders/O-456/cancel\n2. OrderController.cancel(orderId):\n   - Fetch order from repo → exists and status=CANCELLED\n   - Return order as-is (idempotent, no-op)\n3. Response: 200 OK with order body\n\n*Error case - CONFIRMED shipment blocks cancel:*\n1. Request: POST /orders/O-789/cancel\n2. OrderController.cancel(orderId):\n   - Fetch order from repo → exists and status=ACTIVE\n   - Query ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(\"O-789\") → returns [S-3(CONFIRMED)]\n   - Found CONFIRMED shipment → throw ConflictException\n   - Order state unchanged: still ACTIVE\n   - All shipments unchanged\n3. Response: 409 CONFLICT with error code ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT\n\n*Error case - Non-existent order:*\n1. Request: POST /orders/O-missing/cancel\n2. OrderController.cancel(orderId):\n   - Fetch order from repo → null\n   - Throw ResourceNotFoundException\n3. Response: 404 NOT_FOUND with error code ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n\n*Success case - Create shipment for ACTIVE order:*\n1. Request: POST /shipments with orderId=\"O-active\"\n2. ShipmentController.create(request):\n   - Fetch order from repo → exists and status=ACTIVE\n   - Check order not cancelled → pass\n   - Create shipment in CREATED status\n   - Save to repo\n3. Response: 201 CREATED with shipment body\n\n*Error case - Create shipment for CANCELLED order:*\n1. Request: POST /shipments with orderId=\"O-cancelled\"\n2. ShipmentController.create(request):\n   - Fetch order from repo → exists and status=CANCELLED\n   - Order is cancelled → throw ConflictException\n3. Response: 409 CONFLICT with error code ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n*Error case - Create shipment for non-existent order:*\n1. Request: POST /shipments with orderId=\"O-missing\"\n2. ShipmentController.create(request):\n   - Fetch order from repo → null (NOT FOUND)\n   - Keep current behavior (per requirement)\n   - Shipment creation proceeds without order validation? OR validate order exists?\n   \nActually, re-reading requirement: \"Creating a shipment for an order that does not exist keeps its current behaviour.\" This means we should NOT validate order existence for shipment creation. The current code doesn't validate order exists. So we only add the cancelled check.\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n*New OrderControllerTest tests:*\n- `cancel_active_order_succeeds_and_returns_order_with_cancelled_status` - verify cancel transitions ACTIVE→CANCELLED\n- `cancel_active_order_cancels_its_created_shipments` - verify CREATED shipments become CANCELLED, CONFIRMED not touched\n- `cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds_idempotently` - verify re-cancel returns 200 with no changes\n- `cancel_order_with_confirmed_shipment_returns_409_conflict` - verify order/shipments unchanged after failed cancel\n- `cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404` - verify ORDER_NOT_FOUND error code\n\n*New ShipmentControllerTest test:*\n- `create_shipment_for_cancelled_order_returns_409_conflict` - verify ORDER_CANCELLED error code\n\n*Tests to verify order status in GET:*\n- Modify existing tests or add verification in new tests that GET /orders/{orderId} returns status field\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1218,"cache_read_input_tokens":23595,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1218},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_g